> I am a wizard on level 11.  My alignment is Neutral.  When I get on an
> altar to Thoth (neutral) and #offer (sacrifice), nothing happens--
> invariably.  I tried offering dead animals and all kinds of food
> products to no avail.  It has never worked as of Patch level 5.
> It used to work (PL3).  I even tried laying the food at the altar
> before offering.  What is wrong?

The the animals you sacrifice HAS to be "good food". If you wait to long
they become "rotten" or something. If you can't eat it, the gods won't
"eat it".

> 
> Also, I read in this newsgroup that it is possible to change the
> alignment of an altar.  Is this true?  Since I have only found one
> altar in 17 levels, I need to change the one that I have found.
> How do I do it?

When you sacrifice something to an alter with an other alignment you
get the message "You feel a fighting between x and y."

Sometimes your god wins and sometimes he looses.

If he wins NH3 says "You feel the power of <name> increase."
Then you have an alter of your alignment.

